<title>USA: Vivus has shortage of MUSE dosage.</title>
<headline>Vivus has shortage of MUSE dosage.</headline>
<dateline>MENLO PARK, Calif. 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vivus Inc said Thursday it was experiencing a temporary shortage of the 125 microgram dosage of MUSE, its drug to treat erectile dysfunction, due to unexpected strong demand.</p>
<p>Vivus said it has adjusted its manufacturing schedule and will satisfy the demand within a few weeks.</p>
<p>It did not say how the short supply would affect it financially.</p>
<p>Officials at the company were not available for comment.</p>
</text>
